1
00:00:11,022 --> 00:00:15,943
IN THE FOOD CHAIN

2
00:00:17,069 --> 00:00:19,321
[Corne over call]
<i>The final match of the UFS Fight Club</i>

3
00:00:19,405 --> 00:00:21,907
<i>took place at
the old market site last night.</i>

4
00:00:22,575 --> 00:00:24,910
- [grunts]
<i>- Care to guess the winner?</i>

5
00:00:25,619 --> 00:00:28,205
That female rabbit again, I assume?

6
00:00:28,289 --> 00:00:30,332
<i>Yes, name of Kyuu.</i>

7
00:00:30,416 --> 00:00:32,209
<i>She's won 17 fights in a row.</i>

8
00:00:32,293 --> 00:00:34,462
[chuckles] <i>It's getting harder
to bet against her.</i>

9
00:00:34,545 --> 00:00:38,382
[Yahya strains] Yeah, if she can survive
in the Black Market,

10
00:00:38,466 --> 00:00:40,176
she's no ordinary herbivore.

11
00:00:40,885 --> 00:00:44,388
<i>How long has it been since you liberated
the live bait market?</i>

12
00:00:44,472 --> 00:00:46,390
<i>Ten years? Something like that?</i>

13
00:00:46,474 --> 00:00:50,644
<i>It's not like she's stuck there.
So why would Gohin make her an apprentice?</i>

14
00:00:50,728 --> 00:00:53,856
How would I know
the workings of a panda's mind?

15
00:00:55,024 --> 00:00:58,235
<i>I don't know,
but I think this will interest you.</i>

16
00:00:58,319 --> 00:01:00,488
<i>Reports say he has one more apprentice.</i>

17
00:01:01,197 --> 00:01:04,742
<i>Apparently, it's our rogue gray wolf.</i>

18
00:01:04,825 --> 00:01:07,411
Huh? Is that so?

19
00:01:07,495 --> 00:01:10,873
The wolf again. Now, that is interesting.

20
00:01:11,499 --> 00:01:14,710
<i>Our final piece of intel
is on the ivory trafficking case.</i>

21
00:01:14,794 --> 00:01:16,462
<i>We received an anonymous tip.</i>

22
00:01:17,213 --> 00:01:20,132
<i>They sent this photo to us.
Here, take a look.</i>

23
00:01:20,716 --> 00:01:21,759
[strains]

24
00:01:22,927 --> 00:01:24,345
They only took the tusks.

25
00:01:25,513 --> 00:01:28,516
Hmm. Zoom in on that pipe to the right.

26
00:01:29,642 --> 00:01:31,602
[digital zooming sound]

27
00:01:31,685 --> 00:01:34,939
A 10K gate valve... in yellow?

28
00:01:36,524 --> 00:01:39,026
[strains] I think those were
the valves installed

29
00:01:39,109 --> 00:01:41,237
during the redevelopment of Center Street.

30
00:01:41,320 --> 00:01:42,822
- Look into it.
<i>- You got it.</i>

31
00:01:43,489 --> 00:01:45,366
Once you find it, I'll make my move.

32
00:01:50,371 --> 00:01:51,288
[door opens]

33
00:01:51,372 --> 00:01:52,915
- [Els] Legoshi?
- Hmm?

34
00:01:54,250 --> 00:01:57,336
- Oh, my gosh! How are ya?
- I'm okay.

35
00:01:58,254 --> 00:02:00,673
You guys having
a Festival of the Meteor meeting?

36
00:02:00,756 --> 00:02:03,509
Yeah. [sighs] For all the good it's doing.

37
00:02:04,844 --> 00:02:05,886
You've heard, right?

38
00:02:05,970 --> 00:02:08,597
- Separate education split the club in two.
- [Legoshi] Hmm.

39
00:02:08,681 --> 00:02:11,100
So we still haven't come up with
a festival plan.

40
00:02:11,642 --> 00:02:13,561
But if we don't,
we were told they might move it

41
00:02:13,644 --> 00:02:15,688
to some other high school
entirely this year.

42
00:02:17,064 --> 00:02:20,151
I see. Even club activities are in danger.

43
00:02:20,234 --> 00:02:22,528
Why'd you even have to bring it up?

44
00:02:22,611 --> 00:02:24,280
Quite the predicament.

45
00:02:24,363 --> 00:02:26,991
Yeah, we got to do something
before they screw us.

46
00:02:27,074 --> 00:02:29,869
Well, I got to go now.
My boyfriend is waiting for me.

47
00:02:29,952 --> 00:02:32,538
Uh... I... [splutters] Uh, yeah, sure.

48
00:02:32,621 --> 00:02:34,248
- Bye, guys!
- Later.

49
00:02:36,333 --> 00:02:37,585
So, you wanted advice?

50
00:02:39,295 --> 00:02:41,463
[both grunting]

51
00:02:42,089 --> 00:02:43,591
[Legoshi] This is an advice?

52
00:02:43,674 --> 00:02:45,676
[straining] Well, if I said
I needed manual labor,

53
00:02:45,759 --> 00:02:47,887
you wouldn't have shown up, would you?

54
00:02:47,970 --> 00:02:49,763
Why didn't you ask Aoba or Tao?

55
00:02:49,847 --> 00:02:53,225
[groans] Oh, quit whining!
I tried, but they weren't available.

56
00:02:53,934 --> 00:02:55,728
So, what about the herbivores?

57
00:02:56,353 --> 00:02:58,689
I'm sure they would've helped
if you asked 'em.

58
00:02:58,772 --> 00:03:00,065
Yeah, I know.

59
00:03:00,858 --> 00:03:02,067
But, to be honest...

60
00:03:03,277 --> 00:03:04,445
I don't know.

61
00:03:04,528 --> 00:03:07,865
I just feel more at ease
with other carnivores, I guess.

62
00:03:07,948 --> 00:03:10,367
Everyone acts like
it's all the carnivores' fault

63
00:03:10,451 --> 00:03:12,453
that we have separate education now.

64
00:03:12,536 --> 00:03:14,914
It's not like we chose
to be born as carnivores.

65
00:03:14,997 --> 00:03:17,041
Like, come on, give me a freakin' break!

66
00:03:17,124 --> 00:03:18,667
[both strain]

67
00:03:18,751 --> 00:03:20,044
- I mean... [pants]
- Huh?

68
00:03:20,127 --> 00:03:23,213
In spite of all that, I do still love
those little leaf-eaters.

69
00:03:24,256 --> 00:03:25,090
[sighs]

70
00:03:25,716 --> 00:03:28,844
So, hey, what were you thinking,
dropping out of school?

71
00:03:29,762 --> 00:03:31,096
If you were still here,

72
00:03:32,014 --> 00:03:34,308
I'd have a better idea of how not to act.

73
00:03:34,850 --> 00:03:37,978
Watching you fumble worse than me
was always educational.

74
00:03:38,062 --> 00:03:41,774
[Legoshi] <i>Okay, that was a bit rude.
I guess he is still growing up.</i>

75
00:03:46,320 --> 00:03:48,697
[rattling]

76
00:03:48,781 --> 00:03:50,699
[Fudge sighs] So, uh...

77
00:03:51,909 --> 00:03:55,120
Should we even bother with these
if we might not do the festival at all?

78
00:03:55,204 --> 00:03:56,247
Good question.

79
00:03:56,997 --> 00:03:58,624
[inhales deeply] Hey!

80
00:03:59,208 --> 00:04:00,209
Is that Legoshi?

81
00:04:00,793 --> 00:04:03,796
Oh, hey! Great to see you!
What are you doing here?

82
00:04:03,879 --> 00:04:07,299
This mutt may have quit school,
but he never quit the drama club.

83
00:04:07,383 --> 00:04:09,009
What? What is that supposed to mean?

84
00:04:09,093 --> 00:04:11,053
Ah! Hey, Legoshi!

85
00:04:11,136 --> 00:04:13,180
What? Long time no see!

86
00:04:13,764 --> 00:04:14,640
What's this for?

87
00:04:14,723 --> 00:04:17,434
We're going to build
a classroom partition, baby!

88
00:04:17,518 --> 00:04:18,644
Yeah, good idea!

89
00:04:18,727 --> 00:04:20,396
Duh, that's so simple!

90
00:04:20,479 --> 00:04:23,023
We can just split the clubroom
down the middle, right?

91
00:04:23,607 --> 00:04:25,943
Do you think the teachers
are going to be okay with that?

92
00:04:26,527 --> 00:04:28,320
They're not going to have
much of a choice.

93
00:04:28,404 --> 00:04:30,948
You know, now with the festival
on the line.

94
00:04:31,031 --> 00:04:34,118
What? Why, did something happen
at the meeting?

95
00:04:34,201 --> 00:04:37,037
Hey, what do you say
we get this stuff inside?

96
00:04:37,121 --> 00:04:39,456
Uh, sorry. I actually have to
get to work now.

97
00:04:40,165 --> 00:04:42,668
I'll be rooting for you.
I mean that, Bill.

98
00:04:42,751 --> 00:04:46,046
[exclaims, stutters] Don't get all gushy!

99
00:04:46,630 --> 00:04:49,216
- Best of luck, guys.
- Come visit again!

100
00:04:50,634 --> 00:04:52,094
Dude has a job now?

101
00:04:52,177 --> 00:04:54,138
- I wonder what kind of job.
- [Zoe] Hmm.

102
00:04:54,221 --> 00:04:56,181
[Kai] Probably not customer service.

103
00:04:56,932 --> 00:04:58,934
[train chugging past]

104
00:05:04,565 --> 00:05:06,817
[Louis] <i>The raw stink of the Black Market.</i>

105
00:05:08,235 --> 00:05:09,320
<i>Disgusting.</i>

106
00:05:11,238 --> 00:05:14,074
<i>But, it puts my heart at ease.</i>

107
00:05:15,117 --> 00:05:17,286
[inhales deeply] <i>Pathetic.</i>

108
00:05:18,037 --> 00:05:23,000
<i>I wonder what Ibuki would say
if he saw me being so... indecisive.</i>

109
00:05:23,542 --> 00:05:24,710
[bicycle wheels squeal]

110
00:05:24,793 --> 00:05:26,337
- [Legoshi] Hey, Louis!
- Hmm?

111
00:05:26,837 --> 00:05:28,088
Legoshi, hey.

112
00:05:30,632 --> 00:05:33,927
- Look at you, all dressed up.
- [laughs] Yeah, I'm delivering udon.

113
00:05:34,011 --> 00:05:35,929
So-- Uh... [hesitates]

114
00:05:36,013 --> 00:05:38,807
Ah, this thing? [strains softly]

115
00:05:39,933 --> 00:05:42,728
Nice, huh? And this one can't get eaten.

116
00:05:42,811 --> 00:05:45,314
- [gasps, shudders]
- I'm just messing with you.

117
00:05:45,397 --> 00:05:47,524
You don't need to look quite so mortified.

118
00:05:48,108 --> 00:05:48,942
Sorry.

119
00:05:50,069 --> 00:05:53,864
So, what, uh... I mean,
you're in university now, yeah?

120
00:05:53,947 --> 00:05:56,325
Unlike you, I have many obligations.

121
00:05:57,159 --> 00:05:59,953
Hmm? Those aren't fresh scars
on your face, are they?

122
00:06:00,037 --> 00:06:02,873
- [chuckles nervously]
- What a dangerous delivery guy.

123
00:06:02,956 --> 00:06:04,500
No, no, no, I'm not.

124
00:06:04,583 --> 00:06:07,377
You haven't changed at all, have you?
Not one bit.

125
00:06:09,129 --> 00:06:10,714
[Legoshi] <i>And it hits me again.</i>

126
00:06:11,632 --> 00:06:16,595
<i>Why are all the herbivore species
such beautiful, elegant creatures?</i>

127
00:06:18,138 --> 00:06:21,642
<i>If it meant I could live alongside them,
and protect them,</i>

128
00:06:22,935 --> 00:06:27,898
<i>I truly believe that I would be willing
to sacrifice anything.</i>

129
00:06:31,151 --> 00:06:31,985
Hey, Louis.

130
00:06:32,861 --> 00:06:36,323
I think... I think
I just realized something awful.

131
00:06:36,406 --> 00:06:37,241
[Louis] Hmm?

132
00:06:38,367 --> 00:06:39,827
Up until now, I thought

133
00:06:40,619 --> 00:06:42,830
I was driven by my own sense of honor,

134
00:06:42,913 --> 00:06:44,748
taking on the injustices of life,

135
00:06:44,832 --> 00:06:47,167
because that's
a carnivore's responsibility.

136
00:06:48,669 --> 00:06:50,129
But that's not the case.

137
00:06:50,796 --> 00:06:51,713
Turns out,

138
00:06:52,798 --> 00:06:56,260
it's my disposition as a wolf
and my ridiculous fetishes.

139
00:06:56,802 --> 00:06:58,679
I'm just a rampaging pervert.

140
00:06:59,555 --> 00:07:01,723
None of it was for honor or justice.

141
00:07:02,724 --> 00:07:06,103
Well, it took you long enough to realize,
you damn dog.

142
00:07:06,186 --> 00:07:07,020
Huh?

143
00:07:07,813 --> 00:07:10,816
Everybody else already knows
you're just a perverted wolf.

144
00:07:11,483 --> 00:07:14,820
The reason you fell in love with Haru,
is because she was the first herbivore

145
00:07:14,903 --> 00:07:17,573
to ever show you any attention
as a woman, isn't it?

146
00:07:18,574 --> 00:07:20,784
Frankly, that's what all men are like.

147
00:07:20,868 --> 00:07:24,371
And that disposition is also
part of who you are.

148
00:07:25,497 --> 00:07:27,416
But regardless of being a pervert,

149
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:31,712
if there's something you can protect,
then I would call that justice.

150
00:07:32,713 --> 00:07:33,839
Wow, Louis.

151
00:07:34,548 --> 00:07:37,092
If you understand me,
then quit moping, pervert!

152
00:07:37,176 --> 00:07:38,677
- [chuckles nervously]
- Chin up!

153
00:07:41,430 --> 00:07:44,016
- [all groaning]
- To the right.

154
00:07:44,099 --> 00:07:45,100
- Are you sure?
- Seriously?

155
00:07:45,184 --> 00:07:47,060
[Dolph] How do you know
this is the right way?

156
00:07:47,144 --> 00:07:49,563
[Agata] Yeah, the moon is in
the same direction as before.

157
00:07:49,646 --> 00:07:51,982
Just look. The esteemed whiskers
point this way.

158
00:07:52,691 --> 00:07:55,444
[Agata] Is there anyone here
who didn't pluck a whisker?

159
00:07:57,070 --> 00:07:59,281
[Free sighs] Seeing the moon like this

160
00:07:59,364 --> 00:08:02,618
always makes me think
of launching that attack with Louis.

161
00:08:02,701 --> 00:08:04,369
[Victor] I wonder how he's doing.

162
00:08:04,953 --> 00:08:07,789
For a deer, he was always more of a lion
than any of us were.

163
00:08:07,873 --> 00:08:09,791
[chuckles] Yeah.

164
00:08:09,875 --> 00:08:13,462
The current boss did get the Shishi-Gumi
back on its feet in no time,

165
00:08:13,545 --> 00:08:15,881
but it's just not the same
as it used to be.

166
00:08:15,964 --> 00:08:17,090
- [yelps]
- [Dolph] What is it?

167
00:08:17,174 --> 00:08:19,384
- Shit! I stepped in poop!
- [all exclaim in disgust]

168
00:08:19,468 --> 00:08:22,346
- Don't touch me!
- [Jimma groans] Just my luck.

169
00:08:22,429 --> 00:08:23,388
We're turning left.

170
00:08:25,516 --> 00:08:26,683
[amusing music playing]

171
00:08:26,767 --> 00:08:28,894
[Victor] Anyway,
Kines has our group thriving.

172
00:08:28,977 --> 00:08:31,522
Those young folks who got hooked
are coming to the Black Market

173
00:08:31,605 --> 00:08:33,440
looking for raw meat in such numbers

174
00:08:33,524 --> 00:08:35,776
that people are thanking us
for driving business.

175
00:08:35,859 --> 00:08:37,361
Can't argue with results.

176
00:08:37,444 --> 00:08:39,613
- [Dolph scoffs]
- [growls] Watch your mouth!

177
00:08:39,696 --> 00:08:40,948
Look, here's the thing.

178
00:08:41,031 --> 00:08:45,202
We lions are supposed to be dignified
with nobility and firm principles.

179
00:08:45,285 --> 00:08:48,205
And it's like all of that is just gone.

180
00:08:48,288 --> 00:08:49,957
Look at the way he treats his kills.

181
00:08:50,040 --> 00:08:52,543
He doesn't think of those animals
as anything but food.

182
00:08:52,626 --> 00:08:54,836
And the way he eats it
looks so unappetizing.

183
00:08:54,920 --> 00:08:57,589
Yeah, that guy has
no meat consumption manners at all.

184
00:08:57,673 --> 00:08:59,132
Ha, well, you're one to talk.

185
00:08:59,216 --> 00:09:01,677
What do you think Ibuki would say
if he was alive?

186
00:09:02,261 --> 00:09:05,514
Probably just to focus on the next job,
which I feel pretty good about.

187
00:09:05,597 --> 00:09:07,641
The boss mentioned
a Masquerade Night Party,

188
00:09:07,724 --> 00:09:08,725
but what do we do?

189
00:09:08,809 --> 00:09:11,228
Oh, you know. We'll put on a little mask...

190
00:09:11,311 --> 00:09:14,731
[laughs] ...and when no one knows
who we are, we can... [laughs wickedly]

191
00:09:14,815 --> 00:09:16,984
Take out the competition
with a Kines or two, huh?

192
00:09:17,067 --> 00:09:19,736
Sounds more to me like
they'll unveil some new drug.

193
00:09:19,820 --> 00:09:22,281
Either way, we need to hurry
and get out of here.

194
00:09:22,364 --> 00:09:24,283
We got to talk to this Deshico guy.

195
00:09:24,366 --> 00:09:27,911
Otherwise, risk losing an arm or two... Huh?

196
00:09:29,746 --> 00:09:30,706
It's the exit.

197
00:09:31,206 --> 00:09:34,418
Feline intuition really ain't something
to doubt, huh?

198
00:09:35,168 --> 00:09:36,712
- Huh?
- Huh?

199
00:09:36,795 --> 00:09:38,463
[squeaking]

200
00:09:42,009 --> 00:09:44,177
[dramatic classical music playing]

201
00:09:46,179 --> 00:09:48,890
[Deshico] You completed the maze
in a mere three hours.

202
00:09:48,974 --> 00:09:50,684
Well done, Shishi-Gumi.

203
00:09:50,767 --> 00:09:53,770
Don't ever underestimate
the psychic power of our whiskers.

204
00:09:54,271 --> 00:09:57,649
[Deshico] The feline family is said
to be filled with mystique, yes,

205
00:09:57,733 --> 00:10:01,445
but lions, tigers, wildcats, jaguars...

206
00:10:01,987 --> 00:10:04,948
it's laughable that
they could be considered mystical.

207
00:10:05,032 --> 00:10:06,408
They're all far too clumsy.

208
00:10:06,491 --> 00:10:08,368
- [Free] The hell?
- [Deshico] Gentle.

209
00:10:08,452 --> 00:10:11,371
Having been called a spiritual cat myself,

210
00:10:12,039 --> 00:10:14,583
that is simply my opinion,
as Deshico the civet.

211
00:10:14,666 --> 00:10:15,792
[Free] You're just a kid!

212
00:10:15,876 --> 00:10:18,253
Oh, please,
drink your coffee while it's hot.

213
00:10:19,046 --> 00:10:20,547
[all groan softly]

214
00:10:21,173 --> 00:10:22,674
[all sniffing]

215
00:10:25,135 --> 00:10:28,305
[Deshico] Allow me to educate you
on the mystique of the civet.

216
00:10:29,556 --> 00:10:34,269
The coffee beans carefully selected
and eaten by civets are called kopi luwak,

217
00:10:34,353 --> 00:10:36,480
and brew a precious cup of coffee.

218
00:10:36,563 --> 00:10:39,941
In fact, the very coffee you're drinking
was brewed with beans I ate

219
00:10:40,025 --> 00:10:41,943
and later extracted from my excrement.

220
00:10:42,527 --> 00:10:43,487
[all gasp]

221
00:10:43,570 --> 00:10:45,906
You mean it's your... [stammer]

222
00:10:45,989 --> 00:10:47,866
Yes. My poop.

223
00:10:47,949 --> 00:10:50,827
[all gagging]

224
00:10:51,411 --> 00:10:55,123
[chuckles] And the civet's
remarkable nature doesn't stop there.

225
00:10:55,207 --> 00:10:57,417
We also have secretions
from our anal glands,

226
00:10:57,501 --> 00:11:00,462
which are often coveted
as a raw material for perfumes.

227
00:11:01,338 --> 00:11:05,467
Why are these abilities concentrated
solely around our bottoms, I wonder?

228
00:11:06,093 --> 00:11:08,136
I used to agonize over it.

229
00:11:08,220 --> 00:11:09,846
But when things pass through my body,

230
00:11:09,930 --> 00:11:13,058
they transform into something
more beautiful and valuable.

231
00:11:14,059 --> 00:11:16,978
So, now, I'm quite proud
of the creature I am.

232
00:11:17,062 --> 00:11:18,980
[strained growling]

233
00:11:19,815 --> 00:11:22,442
[laughing wickedly]

234
00:11:22,526 --> 00:11:23,693
It's taking effect.

235
00:11:23,777 --> 00:11:25,237
[strained growling]

236
00:11:26,905 --> 00:11:29,658
Coffee is composed of about 98% water,

237
00:11:29,741 --> 00:11:32,786
and the remaining 2% is from the beans.

238
00:11:33,412 --> 00:11:36,665
Only these,
have skeletomuscular narcotic effects

239
00:11:36,748 --> 00:11:38,875
similar to, or even greater than Kines.

240
00:11:38,959 --> 00:11:40,919
So, this is what the boss is after?

241
00:11:42,504 --> 00:11:45,215
This Hyperdrug is comprised of ivory,

242
00:11:45,298 --> 00:11:47,592
little bits of animal flesh and bone...

243
00:11:47,676 --> 00:11:48,510
[bats squeaking]

244
00:11:48,593 --> 00:11:50,971
...all the blood these littles ones gather,

245
00:11:51,513 --> 00:11:53,432
and some of and my kopi luwak.

246
00:11:53,974 --> 00:11:59,438
You blend those all together to create
this perfect black gem, Melda.

247
00:11:59,521 --> 00:12:00,939
[all] Melda?

248
00:12:01,022 --> 00:12:03,024
Also called "deer dung."

249
00:12:03,108 --> 00:12:06,069
It's more potent than anything else
that's been on the market before.

250
00:12:07,028 --> 00:12:09,948
I've already lined up a buyer
for the first batch of these.

251
00:12:10,031 --> 00:12:12,784
And that, of course, would be your boss.

252
00:12:12,868 --> 00:12:16,455
That's what he plans to reveal
at the masquerade. It must be!

253
00:12:18,290 --> 00:12:19,207
[all] Huh?

254
00:12:19,291 --> 00:12:21,460
[music intensifies]

255
00:12:22,961 --> 00:12:24,296
[sniffs]

256
00:12:24,379 --> 00:12:26,548
Ah, that's nice! [chuckles]

257
00:12:26,631 --> 00:12:29,384
Why, thank you. That's a bag of my poop.

258
00:12:30,051 --> 00:12:31,970
- [all exclaiming]
- Cooties! Cooties!

259
00:12:32,053 --> 00:12:34,431
That maze you came through
is made of coffee trees,

260
00:12:34,514 --> 00:12:36,266
and there's a lot of poop in there.

261
00:12:36,349 --> 00:12:39,144
I want you to collect it and return it
to me by the end of the night.

262
00:12:39,227 --> 00:12:40,687
And why should we have to do that?

263
00:12:40,770 --> 00:12:43,398
Yeah, the king of beasts doesn't
go around picking up shit!

264
00:12:43,482 --> 00:12:45,484
Well, I told Melon

265
00:12:45,567 --> 00:12:49,070
I could only produce the drug
if there was someone here to help me.

266
00:12:49,154 --> 00:12:50,238
He didn't say?

267
00:12:50,322 --> 00:12:52,240
[growls] Damn him!

268
00:12:52,324 --> 00:12:54,034
- We're leaving.
- [growls]

269
00:12:54,618 --> 00:12:55,827
Mmm. [inhales]

270
00:12:56,536 --> 00:13:00,248
I wonder if Madara-Gumi or Inari-Gumi
would be interested then.

271
00:13:01,333 --> 00:13:03,543
[all growling]

272
00:13:03,627 --> 00:13:05,378
[music crescendos]

273
00:13:05,462 --> 00:13:07,964
Damn it! Everyone, pluck a whisker!

274
00:13:08,798 --> 00:13:10,800
- [horn honks]
- [engines whirring]

275
00:13:14,971 --> 00:13:17,057
[Legoshi reading] <i>"Legoshi the gray wolf,</i>

276
00:13:17,140 --> 00:13:21,978
<i>we are grateful for your cooperation
in the crackdown on carnivore criminals.</i>

277
00:13:22,062 --> 00:13:25,524
<i>I'd like to take this opportunity
to hear about the state of the city</i>

278
00:13:25,607 --> 00:13:27,359
<i>from you, a brave citizen.</i>

279
00:13:27,442 --> 00:13:30,695
<i>I'm inviting you to dinner, Yahya."</i>

280
00:13:35,784 --> 00:13:37,577
Uh... Here.

281
00:13:39,204 --> 00:13:40,622
What's this?

282
00:13:42,624 --> 00:13:43,625
YAHYA

283
00:13:43,708 --> 00:13:44,668
Oh!

284
00:13:44,751 --> 00:13:46,711
Oh, so sorry to keep you waiting, sir.

285
00:13:47,212 --> 00:13:48,964
[mysterious music playing]

286
00:13:50,799 --> 00:13:54,261
[Legoshi] <i>Just what kind of beast
is Yahya?</i>

287
00:13:55,387 --> 00:13:59,015
<i>What species?
Is he a carnivore? An herbivore?</i>

288
00:14:01,476 --> 00:14:02,352
[elevator dings]

289
00:14:05,105 --> 00:14:06,231
Hmm.

290
00:14:08,191 --> 00:14:11,403
Whoa! [laughs]

291
00:14:12,904 --> 00:14:14,155
Whoa!

292
00:14:16,366 --> 00:14:18,952
[panting]

293
00:14:20,036 --> 00:14:21,162
[chuckles]

294
00:14:21,746 --> 00:14:23,582
<i>Wow! So cool!</i>

295
00:14:24,249 --> 00:14:25,959
<i>That's the Baraena River.</i>

296
00:14:26,042 --> 00:14:28,545
<i>And that must be the Custos Bridge.</i>

297
00:14:28,628 --> 00:14:32,841
[gasps] <i>Hey, there's my apartment!
Wow, it looks so small from up here.</i>

298
00:14:33,466 --> 00:14:34,926
<i>Whoa!</i>

299
00:14:35,510 --> 00:14:37,512
- [Yahya] The city is beautiful at night.
- Huh?

300
00:14:39,556 --> 00:14:41,600
Come on in, Legoshi.

301
00:14:41,683 --> 00:14:42,517
Huh.

302
00:14:43,435 --> 00:14:46,688
Nice to meet you. So are you Mr. Yahya?

303
00:14:47,272 --> 00:14:48,899
Sorry to call you all the way out here.

304
00:14:49,566 --> 00:14:52,110
I hope they were
at least polite to you downstairs.

305
00:14:52,652 --> 00:14:53,653
Yes, they were.

306
00:14:56,531 --> 00:14:58,074
For dinner this evening,

307
00:14:58,158 --> 00:15:01,286
I thought I'd treat you
to the special carrots we grow up here.

308
00:15:02,120 --> 00:15:05,582
Though, perhaps, this cuisine doesn't
appeal to your taste, being a wolf.

309
00:15:05,665 --> 00:15:08,168
It's perfect. Thank you very much.

310
00:15:09,502 --> 00:15:10,462
But, uh...

311
00:15:12,672 --> 00:15:16,509
You're Mr. Yahya,
as in the Beastar, right?

312
00:15:16,593 --> 00:15:18,219
Hmm, why do you ask?

313
00:15:18,303 --> 00:15:21,556
Ah, excuse me.
That was speculation on my part.

314
00:15:22,849 --> 00:15:26,478
You have your own room on the top floor
of the police headquarters.

315
00:15:26,561 --> 00:15:29,022
It's like you're overseeing them,
but mostly...

316
00:15:29,981 --> 00:15:32,859
- these carrots are incredibly delicious!
- [Yahya] Hmm?

317
00:15:32,943 --> 00:15:35,070
They're so sweet
with a hint of earthiness.

318
00:15:35,153 --> 00:15:37,197
Oh, and the flesh is plump and chewy,

319
00:15:37,280 --> 00:15:39,658
and the more you chew...
um, how do I put this?

320
00:15:39,741 --> 00:15:42,202
I don't know, but I've never had
a carrot like this before.

321
00:15:42,744 --> 00:15:44,955
And if you eat such great meals
all the time,

322
00:15:45,038 --> 00:15:46,915
then you must be
a pretty important person.

323
00:15:46,998 --> 00:15:49,960
You know, I... [chuckles]
So, I guess I just figured that...

324
00:15:50,043 --> 00:15:52,712
- I'm sorry.
- Hmm? [laughs]

325
00:15:53,213 --> 00:15:55,298
That's all right. I'm glad you like it.

326
00:15:55,882 --> 00:15:59,344
Yes, the carrots that are grown here
are certainly special.

327
00:16:00,929 --> 00:16:03,181
Managed with
the right water and nutrients,

328
00:16:03,264 --> 00:16:06,393
and kept at the perfect humidity
and temperature at all times.

329
00:16:07,227 --> 00:16:11,022
Only by maintaining a perfect environment
can something perfect can be born.

330
00:16:12,357 --> 00:16:15,193
I think society ought to be the same.
Don't you agree?

331
00:16:16,695 --> 00:16:18,154
[Legoshi] <i>That's settles it.</i>

332
00:16:18,238 --> 00:16:23,451
<i>He hasn't affirmed it,
but Mr. Yahya is probably the Beastar.</i>

333
00:16:24,202 --> 00:16:25,745
<i>But if he is,</i>

334
00:16:25,829 --> 00:16:29,332
<i>I wonder how much responsibility
rests on those towering shoulders.</i>

335
00:16:31,042 --> 00:16:33,753
Before we have dessert,
I'd like to show you something.

336
00:16:37,340 --> 00:16:38,967
[tense music playing]

337
00:16:39,050 --> 00:16:40,969
Understand I'm willing to accept

338
00:16:41,052 --> 00:16:44,055
whatever hardship
or sacrifice is necessary

339
00:16:44,139 --> 00:16:46,224
for the realization of a perfect society.

340
00:16:48,727 --> 00:16:49,936
- Legoshi.
- Mmm?

341
00:16:50,770 --> 00:16:54,482
Tell me, what do you think
the Beastar truly is?

342
00:16:54,566 --> 00:16:55,483
Uh...

343
00:16:56,234 --> 00:16:57,360
I think that...

344
00:16:58,695 --> 00:17:04,159
both herbivores and carnivores
all have their own separate struggles,

345
00:17:04,242 --> 00:17:06,703
but the reason they're able
to still live happily,

346
00:17:06,786 --> 00:17:10,165
is because of the hope that the Beastar
represents to everyone.

347
00:17:10,248 --> 00:17:15,670
So, we... we all try to live up
to this ideal that exists within us.

348
00:17:15,754 --> 00:17:17,213
Or something like that. Yeah.

349
00:17:18,757 --> 00:17:20,341
That's an interesting approach.

350
00:17:21,009 --> 00:17:25,263
However, I'd say the Beastar
is a much more realistic entity.

351
00:17:26,806 --> 00:17:27,891
It's not hope.

352
00:17:29,184 --> 00:17:32,312
A Beastar, you see, exacts law and order.

353
00:17:33,063 --> 00:17:34,314
Law and order?

354
00:17:35,732 --> 00:17:40,695
I mean, I... I actually kind of like seeing
some of the imperfections of our society.

355
00:17:41,362 --> 00:17:43,573
But the fact that
it functions despite them,

356
00:17:44,199 --> 00:17:45,825
is all thanks to you, isn't it?

357
00:17:45,909 --> 00:17:47,035
That's amazing.

358
00:17:47,702 --> 00:17:51,372
[Yahya] <i>What a polite,
agreeable young wolf he is.</i>

359
00:17:51,456 --> 00:17:52,665
<i>Almost carefree.</i>

360
00:17:53,708 --> 00:17:55,168
<i>This kid gets on my nerves.</i>

361
00:17:57,212 --> 00:17:58,922
But I'm sure you've wondered.

362
00:17:59,005 --> 00:18:01,257
So, let me ask you directly.

363
00:18:01,341 --> 00:18:04,094
Do you not find it strange
that one horse alone

364
00:18:04,177 --> 00:18:06,888
has the strength to battle
the evils of the world?

365
00:18:06,971 --> 00:18:08,598
So, what, do you work out or something?

366
00:18:08,681 --> 00:18:11,768
[scoffs] I do. But I still require
an additional source of energy.

367
00:18:11,851 --> 00:18:12,727
[Legoshi] Hmm.

368
00:18:13,311 --> 00:18:14,854
When you become a Beastar,

369
00:18:14,938 --> 00:18:18,149
you have one wish granted,
no matter what it may be.

370
00:18:20,860 --> 00:18:22,570
Even, for instance,

371
00:18:22,654 --> 00:18:24,989
if you want to turn the carnivores
you've punished

372
00:18:25,073 --> 00:18:27,033
into fertilizer for your garden,

373
00:18:27,117 --> 00:18:28,576
that's perfectly acceptable.

374
00:18:29,160 --> 00:18:31,412
And with your previous record
of devouring...

375
00:18:33,665 --> 00:18:34,874
[gasps]

376
00:18:35,458 --> 00:18:38,837
...these carrots, which have devoured
all those animal nutrients,

377
00:18:38,920 --> 00:18:41,131
must have been especially delicious.

378
00:18:41,214 --> 00:18:42,841
[gasping]

379
00:18:42,924 --> 00:18:44,008
Oh, my...

380
00:18:45,385 --> 00:18:46,427
Speechless, are we?

381
00:18:46,928 --> 00:18:48,638
[grunts, groans]

382
00:18:51,182 --> 00:18:52,642
[groaning]

383
00:18:56,062 --> 00:18:57,105
[yelps]

384
00:18:57,188 --> 00:19:01,609
Surely, you don't have any intention
of criticizing me about this, Legoshi.

385
00:19:01,693 --> 00:19:04,237
I've read all about you, my friend.

386
00:19:04,320 --> 00:19:08,616
About how you willingly ate the flesh
and blood of your conscious classmate,

387
00:19:08,700 --> 00:19:12,787
to somewhat ironically win a duel
against a devourer classmate.

388
00:19:12,871 --> 00:19:14,998
- That's some determination.
- [groaning]

389
00:19:15,081 --> 00:19:19,460
But can consider this
good conduct, I wonder?

390
00:19:19,544 --> 00:19:20,920
[grunting]

391
00:19:22,172 --> 00:19:24,257
<i>What do you think, Gosha?</i>

392
00:19:25,758 --> 00:19:27,051
[grunts]

393
00:19:27,719 --> 00:19:30,430
Do you understand what you're doing here?
No one is going to accept

394
00:19:30,513 --> 00:19:33,141
a mammal and a reptile
starting a mixed blood family.

395
00:19:33,224 --> 00:19:34,809
[groans] That may be.

396
00:19:35,351 --> 00:19:38,855
But I also understand
that every family has its own troubles.

397
00:19:39,439 --> 00:19:42,317
And whatever they are,
she and I will face them together!

398
00:19:42,400 --> 00:19:45,153
There's a true happiness
that exists out there.

399
00:19:45,236 --> 00:19:47,947
That's what I've been searching for
for my entire life!

400
00:19:48,781 --> 00:19:52,327
I never imagined that someone
could love a venomous lizard.

401
00:19:52,410 --> 00:19:53,703
Forgive me, my friend.

402
00:19:54,370 --> 00:19:56,831
[Yahya] <i>I'm afraid I can't do that, Gosha.</i>

403
00:19:57,373 --> 00:20:00,418
<i>And now, the choice you made
out of a hunger for love,</i>

404
00:20:00,501 --> 00:20:04,422
<i>had led to your dear grandchild
to the sole of my boot,</i>

405
00:20:04,505 --> 00:20:07,133
<i>to be judged by my absolute authority.</i>

406
00:20:09,010 --> 00:20:11,179
[groaning]

407
00:20:12,263 --> 00:20:14,515
Let me explain something to you.

408
00:20:18,394 --> 00:20:19,771
Out here in the real world,

409
00:20:19,854 --> 00:20:22,607
the first thing one must do
to escape a crisis,

410
00:20:22,690 --> 00:20:24,651
is show absolute sincerity.

411
00:20:24,734 --> 00:20:26,152
[stutters] Sincerity?

412
00:20:27,737 --> 00:20:29,864
I want you to beg for my forgiveness.

413
00:20:30,615 --> 00:20:32,116
Regardless of the reason,

414
00:20:32,200 --> 00:20:37,205
a Beastar cannot excuse the devouring
of a living herbivore, you must realize.

415
00:20:38,122 --> 00:20:42,710
However, if you're willing to grovel
here on the ground before me,

416
00:20:42,794 --> 00:20:47,090
with a sincere apology to me for ever
being born a carnivore in the first place,

417
00:20:47,674 --> 00:20:49,968
then at least you won't end up
as fertilizer,

418
00:20:50,051 --> 00:20:52,136
like the many beasts who came before you.

419
00:20:53,346 --> 00:20:55,598
Now, what do you say?

420
00:20:58,101 --> 00:21:01,896
[Legoshi] <i>I only did it because
I would've never beaten Riz otherwise.</i>

421
00:21:01,980 --> 00:21:05,900
<i>But, an apology for being born
a carnivore?</i>

422
00:21:06,943 --> 00:21:08,987
[Yahya] <i>Time to settle this, Gosha.</i>

423
00:21:09,821 --> 00:21:14,158
<i>Which one of us is wrong?
And which is righteous?</i>

424
00:21:19,163 --> 00:21:23,293
For being born a carnivore,
and for eating my friend's leg...

425
00:21:24,752 --> 00:21:25,628
I'm sorry.

426
00:21:27,422 --> 00:21:29,299
Although I had consent,

427
00:21:30,091 --> 00:21:31,676
I did something unforgivable.

428
00:21:31,759 --> 00:21:33,553
- [squelching]
- [Legoshi groans]

429
00:21:34,512 --> 00:21:36,306
I try to atone for it every day.

430
00:21:36,389 --> 00:21:38,474
- [squelching]
- [pants, grunts]

431
00:21:39,267 --> 00:21:40,768
I plan to live with what I've done.

432
00:21:41,561 --> 00:21:44,147
[panting, grunting]

433
00:21:47,108 --> 00:21:48,443
[slurring] And that's why...

434
00:21:48,526 --> 00:21:50,445
[panting]

435
00:21:50,528 --> 00:21:51,446
...from now on...

436
00:21:51,529 --> 00:21:53,573
[tense music playing]

437
00:21:54,240 --> 00:21:55,575
I don't need fangs!

438
00:21:55,658 --> 00:21:57,869
- [fangs clatter]
- [breathing heavily]

439
00:21:57,952 --> 00:21:59,912
[tense music crescendos]

440
00:22:00,997 --> 00:22:02,123
[closing theme song playing]

441
00:22:02,206 --> 00:22:04,792
<i>♪ Just like a new melody ♪</i>

442
00:22:04,876 --> 00:22:08,296
<i>♪ Keep it beating on and on ♪</i>

443
00:22:09,464 --> 00:22:12,508
<i>♪ I don't want to live without it ♪</i>

444
00:22:13,384 --> 00:22:15,762
<i>♪ You give me the strength inside ♪</i>

445
00:22:17,764 --> 00:22:20,975
<i>♪ Some things aren't meant to be ♪</i>

446
00:22:21,059 --> 00:22:23,561
<i>♪ You say it like you know ♪</i>

447
00:22:23,644 --> 00:22:26,189
<i>♪ But I really want you ♪</i>

448
00:22:27,607 --> 00:22:31,527
<i>♪ I want you to see it the way I do ♪</i>

449
00:22:32,570 --> 00:22:36,783
<i>♪ 'Cause every time I think about you ♪</i>

450
00:22:37,408 --> 00:22:40,119
<i>♪ My heartbeat goes a-risin' ♪</i>

451
00:22:40,203 --> 00:22:44,707
- <i>♪ And I just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

452
00:22:44,791 --> 00:22:46,751
- <i>♪ Till I... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

453
00:22:46,834 --> 00:22:48,044
<i>♪ Till I die ♪</i>

454
00:22:48,127 --> 00:22:52,548
<i>♪ There's nothing
That can beat like this ♪</i>

455
00:22:53,216 --> 00:22:56,511
<i>♪ Faster as I close my eyes ♪</i>

456
00:22:56,594 --> 00:23:00,807
- <i>♪ Just want to feel like this ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

457
00:23:00,890 --> 00:23:02,725
- <i>♪ Till the... ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

458
00:23:02,809 --> 00:23:04,060
<i>♪ Till the night ♪</i>

459
00:23:04,852 --> 00:23:08,731
<i>♪ Now as long as you are here by my sid</i> e ♪

460
00:23:09,232 --> 00:23:10,566
<i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>

461
00:23:10,650 --> 00:23:12,819
<i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>

462
00:23:13,486 --> 00:23:16,280
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

463
00:23:17,406 --> 00:23:19,367
<i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

464
00:23:19,450 --> 00:23:24,330
{\an8}- <i>♪ Ooh-ooh-ooh ♪</i>
- <i>♪ Walking on, on, walking on, on ♪</i>

465
00:23:25,414 --> 00:23:28,876
{\an8}- <i>♪ Run, run, run ♪</i>
- <i>♪ I keep walking on ♪</i>
